<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>Latest news from the Middle East, daily international news reports - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24’s coverage and analyses of political and social issues across the Middle East, including Egypt, the Gulf states, Iraq, Israel, Jordan, Lebanon, Saudi Arabia, Syria, Yemen and beyond.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/</link><lastBuildDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 02:48:14 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israel intensifies South Lebanon strikes, killing 13 after weeks-long lull</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260907-israeli-strikes-south-lebanon-violence</link><description>
Israel launched a wave of airstrikes across southern Lebanon, killing 13 people, including women and children, Lebanon’s health ministry said on Monday, marking an escalation after weeks of relative calm. Israel said it would continue targeting Iran-backed Hezbollah over alleged ceasefire violations. Hezbollah has not commented on the strikes.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/61e9ca92-6766-11f1-a698-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B6YE6TE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/61e9ca92-6766-11f1-a698-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B6YE6TE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0ec8837e-ab01-11f1-8ab2-0b475800e741</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 21:32:03 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/61e9ca92-6766-11f1-a698-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B6YE6TE.jpg">© Abbas Fakih, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israel warns of 'full-scale war' if Palestinian Authority launches Oct. 7-style attack</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260907-israel-warns-of-full-scale-war-if-palestinian-authority-launches-oct-7-style-attack</link><description>
Israel on Monday threatened a “full-scale war” against the Palestinian Authority if it believed the West Bank-based body was preparing an attack on Israeli forces or settlements resembling Hamas’s October 7, 2023 assault. The warning was denounced by Palestinian authorities as an attempt to fuel the conflict during the Israeli election season.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8a5ad172-aae3-11f1-86fb-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6GC4RR.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8a5ad172-aae3-11f1-86fb-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6GC4RR.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">276750a0-aadd-11f1-973d-9175e80f4543</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 18:08:40 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8a5ad172-aae3-11f1-86fb-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6GC4RR.jpg">© Zain Jaafar, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israeli strikes on southern Lebanon kill 11</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-israeli-strikes-on-southern-lebanon-kill-11</link><description>
Israeli strikes ⁠on a ​southern Lebanese town early on Monday killed at least 11 people including two children ​and two medics, Lebanon's state news agency said. Israel has intensified its bombardment of south Lebanon in recent days despite a June ceasefire that was meant ​to halt fighting ‌between the Israeli military and Lebanese armed ⁠group Hezbollah. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6c410c12-aac3-11f1-ba63-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/minilebanon.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6c410c12-aac3-11f1-ba63-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/minilebanon.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">76dbfbfa-aac3-11f1-b3a5-39bbc4f04cbf</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 14:10:28 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>UN rapporteur says Israeli rubble-clearing in Gaza could erase 'atrocity crimes' evidence</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260907-un-rapporteur-says-israeli-rubble-clearing-in-gaza-could-erase-atrocity-crimes-evidence</link><description>
The United Nations Special Rapporteur Francesca Albanese warned on Monday that the large-scale rubble removal in parts of Gaza under Israeli control could risk erasing "evidence relevant to the investigation of alleged international crimes". 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/22ab0c38-aac3-11f1-8592-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26236599212384.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/22ab0c38-aac3-11f1-8592-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26236599212384.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d529b836-aaba-11f1-8535-e7288cd5752f</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 12:51:23 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/22ab0c38-aac3-11f1-8592-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26236599212384.jpg">© Jehad Alshrafi, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Several killed in Israeli strikes in southern Lebanon</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260907-middle-east-live-israel-army-orders-evacuation-of-zone-in-south-lebanon-ahead-of-strikes</link><description>
At ⁠least ​11 ​people were killed, including two infants, were injured ⁠in Israeli strikes on ​a ‌residential building in ‌a town ​in southern Lebanon early on Monday, ​Lebanon's ​state ​news agency ​reported. The Israeli army had demanded early Monday that residents of Deir Zahrani in southern Lebanon leave a specific zone ahead of strikes against Iran-backed Hezbollah. Follow our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/90c16efa-6fcd-11f1-9268-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B83C3LW.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/90c16efa-6fcd-11f1-9268-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B83C3LW.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4b743ea2-aa58-11f1-8fe0-91af53a39a4b</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 01:13:12 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/90c16efa-6fcd-11f1-9268-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B83C3LW.jpg">© Fadel Itani, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israeli strikes kill four in Lebanon after alleged Hezbollah drone launch</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260906-israeli-strikes-kill-four-in-lebanon-after-alleged-hezbollah-drone-launch</link><description>
Israeli air strikes on southern Lebanon Sunday killed four people, two of them women, the country's health ministry said. Israel's military said that the strikes were a response to an alleged Hezbollah drone launch targeting troops in the Israeli-occupied "security zone" in the country's south.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2b6c4208-a9cc-11f1-97b3-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26249260716697.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2b6c4208-a9cc-11f1-97b3-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26249260716697.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">60dd8fba-a9cb-11f1-b90f-a327c3f340e1</guid><pubDate>Sun, 06 Sep 2026 08:49:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2b6c4208-a9cc-11f1-97b3-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26249260716697.jpg">© Mohammed Zaatari, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>US ambassador to Israel visits Palestinian town hit by West Bank settler violence</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260905-us-ambassador-to-israel-visits-palestinian-town-hit-by-west-bank-settler-violence</link><description>
US ambassador to Israel Mike Huckabee on Saturday visited Turmus Ayya, a Palestinian town in the Israeli-occupied West Bank that has been repeatedly targeted by Israeli settler violence. Huckabee, a staunch supporter of Israel and its illegal settlements in the Palestinian territory, said that it was in the Israeli government's interests to take action against violent settlers. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dce040ce-a91e-11f1-8989-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-05T083710Z-194611372-RC2WCNA3NVQT-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-SETTLERS-USA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dce040ce-a91e-11f1-8989-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-05T083710Z-194611372-RC2WCNA3NVQT-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-SETTLERS-USA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9fdd2e76-a91e-11f1-b618-498e4f3d2836</guid><pubDate>Sat, 05 Sep 2026 12:19:19 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dce040ce-a91e-11f1-8989-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-05T083710Z-194611372-RC2WCNA3NVQT-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-SETTLERS-USA.jpg">© Ammar Awad, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>US military says it struck 3 Iranian oil tankers after missile attacks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260905-middle-east-live-israeli-strikes-on-south-and-east-lebanon-kill-three-people</link><description>
The US military said on Saturday it had struck and destroyed three Iranian oil tankers after Navy warships were targeted with missiles, adding that no American personnel ​were ​harmed. Earlier, Tehran accused the US of attacking an Iranian tanker near Kharg Island in the Persian Gulf, a key oil terminal. Follow our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/96284e10-a932-11f1-bc0d-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Capture-d-%C3%A9cran-2026-09-05-160135.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/96284e10-a932-11f1-bc0d-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Capture-d-%C3%A9cran-2026-09-05-160135.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9e9b199a-a8e4-11f1-9cc9-ed32b8bec523</guid><pubDate>Sat, 05 Sep 2026 05:01:24 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/96284e10-a932-11f1-bc0d-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Capture-d-%C3%A9cran-2026-09-05-160135.png">© Centcom, X</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israel's West Bank camp displacements could be crime against humanity, UN says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260904-israel-s-west-bank-camp-displacements-could-be-crime-against-humanity-un-says</link><description>
The Israeli government's forced displacement of the entire populations of three West Bank refugee camps in January 2025 could amount to crimes against humanity, a UN report warned Friday. More than 33,000 Palestinians forced out of the Jenin, Nur Shams and Tulkarm camps have not been permitted to return home. Israel slammed the report for "spreading misinformation".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7cd77414-a878-11f1-bbf1-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25050234334915.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7cd77414-a878-11f1-bbf1-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25050234334915.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9d75c9d6-a879-11f1-9f3f-9d5ffd1b430b</guid><pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 16:26:55 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7cd77414-a878-11f1-bbf1-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25050234334915.jpg">© Majdi Mohammed, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israeli army has seized Lebanon's key Ali al-Taher ridge from Hezbollah</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260904-israel-says-it-has-seized-lebanon-key-ali-al-taher-ridge-from-hezbollah</link><description>
Israel has seized the strategically placed Ali al-Taher ridge in southern Lebanon from Hezbollah fighters, Defence Minister Israel Katz said Friday. The Iran-aligned Shiite group did not confirm losing the highland, which sits around 10 kilometres from the border with Israel and was pummelled by Israeli strikes in recent weeks despite a ceasefire.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d6fd5dd8-a863-11f1-8979-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7CP76M.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d6fd5dd8-a863-11f1-8979-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7CP76M.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3d129fd8-a851-11f1-aadd-c1a3999cb03a</guid><pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 13:27:50 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d6fd5dd8-a863-11f1-8979-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7CP76M.jpg">© Kawnat Haju, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>New fears of oil supply disruption as US-Iran hostilities resume</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-new-fears-of-oil-supply-disruption-as-us-iran-hostilities-resume</link><description>
Renewed hostilities between the United States and Iran have brought back fears of oil supply disruption. Prices are on track for their steepest weekly gain since mid-July, up 7.6%, as the US-Iran war enters its seventh month. Twenty-five percent of the world's oil supply comes through the Strait of Hormuz, which has been blocked since the beginning of the war. FRANCE 24's international affairs editor Philip Turle gives more details.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d161bcbc-a844-11f1-8204-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-18958653076a9a924e5802b3-90615016.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d161bcbc-a844-11f1-8204-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-18958653076a9a924e5802b3-90615016.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">12b6c7cc-a843-11f1-8018-e71901705b94</guid><pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 09:56:46 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Trump says Iran war is 'small potatoes', Israel strikes southern Lebanon</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260904-middle-east-live-south-korea-prepares-for-military-deployment-in-strait-of-hormuz</link><description>
President Donald Trump on Friday said the Iran war was "small potatoes" for the US, a day after Vice President JD Vance said he wouldn't describe the conflict as a war. In Lebanon, an Israeli strike killed two people in the south, state media reported. Read about the day’s events as they unfolded on our liveblog. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f9606e9c-91ed-11f1-80ab-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26218729542918.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f9606e9c-91ed-11f1-80ab-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26218729542918.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">eb75ede6-a801-11f1-8538-997226343bce</guid><pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 02:56:56 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f9606e9c-91ed-11f1-80ab-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26218729542918.jpg">© Alex Brandon, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Truth or Fake</category><title>No, UN chief Guterres did not call Francesca Albanese 'out of control'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20260903-no-un-chief-guterres-did-not-call-francesca-albanese-out-of-control</link><description>
Pro-Israel lobby group UN Watch has alleged that UN Secretary-General Antonio Guterres referred to Francesca Albanese, the UN's Special Rapporteur on Palestine, as "out of control", saying he'd previously called her a "horrible woman". But Guterres named no one in his remarks. He said "many" independent rapporteurs were "totally out of control", without singling out any individual. The UN has since said that linking the comment specifically to Albanese is a "misreading" of his remarks. Vedika Bahl fact-checks.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/faa1685e-a7ca-11f1-a357-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-447843536a99c5e4f335f7-83392847.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/faa1685e-a7ca-11f1-a357-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-447843536a99c5e4f335f7-83392847.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e3d9dddc-a7c9-11f1-91c8-c9b691556019</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 19:34:29 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Vedika BAHL</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Anti-Christian murder in Syria? No indication he was killed because of his faith</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260903-anti-christian-murder-syria-no-indication-killed-faith</link><description>
A Christian man by the name of Nader Boulos Tannous was murdered in Homs, Syria on August 15, 2026. After his death, Israel, Greece and Cyprus were quick to denounce what they called an anti-Christian act. Several days later however, authorities in Homs said the suspect had admitted killing Tannous as part of a personal dispute going back to 2012.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/efbc11e2-a2f6-11f1-bfe9-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Mod%C3%A8le-1920-x-1080-11-2.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/efbc11e2-a2f6-11f1-bfe9-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Mod%C3%A8le-1920-x-1080-11-2.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">03e99b86-a6a7-11f1-a89b-73cec2680c44</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 17:00:20 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/efbc11e2-a2f6-11f1-bfe9-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Mod%C3%A8le-1920-x-1080-11-2.png">© Montage by the Observers </source><dc:creator>The FRANCE 24 Observers</dc:creator></item><item><category>Tête à tête</category><title>Israeli attacks in West Bank at 'unprecedented' level, PNI leader Barghouti says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20260903-israeli-attacks-in-west-bank-at-unprecedented-level-pni-leader-barghouti-says</link><description>
In an interview with FRANCE 24, the secretary general of the Palestinian National Initiative (PNI) party Mustafa Barghouti said the level of Israeli attacks on Palestinians in the West Bank had become "totally unprecedented". With tensions escalating, activists accuse settlers of operating with total impunity. "Their goal is clear: it is ethnic cleansing," Barghouti stated, calling Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's reaction to the attacks hypocritical.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b9a8929c-a6b1-11f1-9d8d-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/BARGHOUTI.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b9a8929c-a6b1-11f1-9d8d-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/BARGHOUTI.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cad2f05e-a6b0-11f1-b09a-eb672b3e2093</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 13:26:12 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Marc PERELMAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Has Iran modified its rocket systems to fire mines into the Strait of Hormuz?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260903-has-iran-modified-its-rocket-systems-to-fire-mines-into-the-strait-of-hormuz</link><description>
Fighting escalated in the Middle East over the weekend after US airstrikes on Sunday targeted Iranian rocket launchers on the island of Larak. The exchange of fire was instigated by the US in retaliation against Iran’s new capabilities for firing mines from rockets into the Strait of Hormuz. Iran’s use of rocket launchers to deploy sea mines into the strategic waterway would be unprecedented, but not implausible. Even so, some analysts remain sceptical.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5679bf30-a61a-11f1-87c2-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/fajr-5.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5679bf30-a61a-11f1-87c2-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/fajr-5.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1e5d00dc-a708-11f1-ae6a-7df714f7ef0c</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 05:57:20 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5679bf30-a61a-11f1-87c2-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/fajr-5.jpg">© Hadi Yazdani, AP</source><dc:creator>Sébastian SEIBT</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Iran hits US targets in Mideast, wedding strikes being probed, Vance says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260903-iran-hits-us-targets-as-washington-says-probing-wedding-strike</link><description>
Iran said on Thursday it hit US military bases in Kuwait and the UAE in retaliation for a US strike on a wedding party that killed four people and injured nearly 70. While the US military has reiterated that it never targets civilians, Vice President JD Vance said the strike was being investigated.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/decdf7b2-a7c7-11f1-9862-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/9ab7109247ff702b409b67379038daf960c895ec.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/decdf7b2-a7c7-11f1-9862-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/9ab7109247ff702b409b67379038daf960c895ec.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0081b310-a757-11f1-8a5a-27e4a23fc3aa</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 05:19:13 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/decdf7b2-a7c7-11f1-9862-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/9ab7109247ff702b409b67379038daf960c895ec.jpg">© AFP via US Navy handout</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Toppling Iran’s Islamic regime ‘within reach’, Netanyahu says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260903-mideast-live-kuwait-army-says-intercepting-missile-drone-attack-from-iran</link><description>
Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu on Thursday voiced confidence that Iran's Islamic republic could soon fall, saying it was weaker than ever. Earlier, Iran's army said it targeted US bases in the UAE and Kuwait. Follow our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded. 
